meta {
  name: Register push token
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

put {
  url: {{api}}/me/devices/current/push-token
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "token": "{{pushToken}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Gives the device you signed in from a push token: 204, and 204 again for the same token. The device is the one your Login described, so there is no id in the path. A token is a secret (whoever holds it can make that phone show a notification): set it as the secret `pushToken`, never in a file.

  A session whose sign-in described no device, or one that has ended, is 404. A token that is blank, has whitespace in it or is over 1024 characters is 422 on token. Logging out forgets it. Until slice N3 nothing sends a push, and production writes a push to its log rather than sending it (ADR-0044).
}
